  "body": "## What\nThe operator screen (plan \u00a73.5), transplanted from the legacy kernel's `tui/ui.rs`/`model.rs` patterns and rebuilt on the `Source` trait the skeleton defined, so it lands before live data:\n- `src/tui/mod.rs`: `run(Box<dyn Source>)`; loader thread + mpsc (snapshot every 2 s), 100 ms crossterm poll, `RestoreTerminal` drop guard, paint-before-first-data; not a tty or `TERM=dumb` \u2192 `plain()` and exit 0; `BF_TUI_ONCE=1` \u2192 one frame to stdout (tests/CI).\n- `src/tui/model.rs`: three views (Agents, Board, PRs), `Row{id,label,human,raw}`, `replace_rows` keeping the selection by id across snapshots, step/enter/back, `/` filter, focus, overlays (help, `y/N` confirm, one-line input), busy-first sort, status lines, `plain()`.\n- `src/tui/ui.rs`: `Palette::{none,truecolor,indexed,detect}` (`NO_COLOR` wins), 2-line status | 45/55 list+detail (vertical < 85 cols) | footer, overlays, follow-tail scroll clamp.\n- `src/tui/text.rs`: `terminal_text` strips C0/C1 controls, ESC/OSC sequences and Unicode bidi overrides before anything reaches the terminal.\n- Keys as specified: `1 2 3`, `Tab/BackTab`, `j/k/\u2191/\u2193`, `Enter`, `Esc`, `/`, `J`, `r`, `t`, `?`, `q`/`Ctrl+C`; Agents `x` (confirm \u2192 `Source::stop`) and `n` (note to agent); Board `n`, `x` (confirm \u2192 expire claim); PRs `o` prints the URL.\n- `tests/tui.rs` (8): `TestBackend` renders at 80x24 / 60x30 / 100x30 asserting titles, hint line, `unknown` and `waiting: x` labels, the stale-PRs warning, help overlay, scroll clamp, and all-Reset cells under `Palette::none()`; model step/enter/back, filter, selection kept by id, busy-first; sanitizer; `run` under `BF_TUI_ONCE`.\n- `tests/cli_skeleton.rs`: bare `bf` without a tty now expects exit 0.\n\nNo new dependencies (ratatui 0.30.2 / crossterm 0.29.0 were pinned in the skeleton).\n\n## Acceptance (plan \u00a74, PR 6)\n`cargo test tui::` TestBackend passes \u2714; `BF_TUI_ONCE=1 bf` prints one frame with the screen title and footer \u2714; `bf </dev/null` prints the plain snapshot, exit 0 \u2714. Local: fmt/clippy `-D warnings` clean; 24 tests; `bash scripts/check` EXIT 0 (15 s isolated).\n\nKnown nits (left for the wiring PR): the ONCE frame shows the current view only; the status line is clipped at 80 columns (no wrap). This PR shares `tests/cli_skeleton.rs` with the board PR; whichever merges second rebases (one-line conflict).\n\n## Review\nReviewer must be a different vendor (grok, codex or cursor): `REVIEW: approve <head-sha>` via `gh pr review --comment`, then `gh pr merge --rebase --delete-branch`.\n\nbf-author: claude/claude-orch \u00b7 bf-claim: AGENT_CHAT.md 2026-09-18T16:34Z\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
